<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<AddRazorSupportForMvc>true</AddRazorSupportForMvc>
		<AssemblyName>DevInstance.BlazorToolkit</AssemblyName>
		<RootNamespace>DevInstance.BlazorToolkit</RootNamespace>
		<Configurations>Debug;Release;</Configurations>
		<Copyright>Copyright 2024-2026 DevInstance LLC</Copyright>
		<Company>DevInstance LLC</Company>
		<Authors>Yuriy Frankiv</Authors>
		<Description>BlazorToolkit is a comprehensive set of tools designed to enhance the development of Blazor applications. It provides a suite of utilities and services that streamline common tasks, allowing developers to focus on building rich, interactive web applications.</Description>
		<Version>10.6.0</Version>
		<AssemblyVersion>10.6.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
		<FileVersion>10.6.0.0</FileVersion>
		<StaticWebAssetProjectMode>Default</StaticWebAssetProjectMode>
		<BlazorDisableThrowNavigationException>true</BlazorDisableThrowNavigationException>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
		<PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>True</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
		<SignAssembly>False</SignAssembly>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<Title>Blazor Toolkit</Title>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://devinstance.net/engineering/blazortoolkit</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/devInstance/BlazorToolkit/</RepositoryUrl>
		<PackageTags>tools, blazor</PackageTags>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>10.6.0
- BREAKING: the UI components (ErrorMessageBanner, PageProgress, LoadingProgress, DataPager, ModelDataPager, SortableHeader, BlazorToolkitPageLayout) moved to the new DevInstance.BlazorToolkit.Components package. Add that package if you use any of them; the namespace (DevInstance.BlazorToolkit.Components) is unchanged, so no code changes are needed.
- ServiceExecutionHostComponent stays in this package.
- Watch out: if the Components package is missing, Razor does not fail the build. It only emits warning RZ10012 and the components silently render nothing. Add &lt;WarningsAsErrors&gt;%24(WarningsAsErrors);RZ10012&lt;/WarningsAsErrors&gt; to your project while upgrading.
See https://github.com/devInstance/BlazorToolkit/blob/master/docs/USAGE.md#ui-components</PackageReleaseNotes>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="icon.png">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
		<None Include="..\README.md">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
		<None Include="..\LICENSE">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<!-- The Components package lives in a subfolder of this project's directory; keep it out of the core assembly. -->
	<ItemGroup>
		<Compile Remove="DevInstance.BlazorToolkit.Components\**" />
		<Content Remove="DevInstance.BlazorToolkit.Components\**" />
		<None Remove="DevInstance.BlazorToolkit.Components\**" />
		<EmbeddedResource Remove="DevInstance.BlazorToolkit.Components\**" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="DevInstance.LogScope" Version="10.1.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="DevInstance.WebServiceToolkit.Common" Version="10.3.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" Version="12.1.1" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly" Version="10.0.12" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="10.0.12" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Http" Version="10.0.12" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Update="LICENSE">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <Folder Include="wwwroot\" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
